 "sq": [
  {
   "_id": 12513,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"701\" data-start=\"529\">Contiguous memory allocation is a memory management technique where each process is allocated a single continuous block of memory space.<br data-end=\"684\" data-start=\"681\" />\n<strong data-end=\"699\" data-start=\"684\">Advantages:</strong></p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"898\" data-start=\"702\">\n\t<li data-end=\"725\" data-start=\"702\">\n\t<p data-end=\"725\" data-start=\"704\">Simple to implement</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"798\" data-start=\"726\">\n\t<p data-end=\"798\" data-start=\"728\">Fast memory access due to contiguous addressing<br data-end=\"778\" data-start=\"775\" />\n\t<strong data-end=\"796\" data-start=\"778\">Disadvantages:</strong></p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"834\" data-start=\"799\">\n\t<p data-end=\"834\" data-start=\"801\">Leads to external fragmentation</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"898\" data-start=\"835\">\n\t<p data-end=\"898\" data-start=\"837\">Difficult to allocate memory for large or growing processes</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p data-end=\"925\" data-start=\"900\">&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"923\" data-start=\"903\">Mark Allocation:</strong></p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"1061\" data-start=\"926\">\n\t<li data-end=\"946\" data-start=\"926\">\n\t<p data-end=\"946\" data-start=\"928\">Definition &ndash; 30%</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"977\" data-start=\"947\">\n\t<p data-end=\"977\" data-start=\"949\">Two valid advantages &ndash; 20%</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1011\" data-start=\"978\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1011\" data-start=\"980\">Two valid disadvantages &ndash; 20%</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1061\" data-start=\"1012\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1061\" data-start=\"1014\">Clarity and structure &ndash; 30%</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC202J",
   "LEVEL": 1,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>What is contiguous memory allocation? List its advantages and disadvantages.</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 402,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 12513
  },
  {
   "_id": 12514,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"2492\" data-start=\"2241\">Best Fit tries to minimize leftover space by choosing the smallest possible block, but this often leaves many small, unusable holes in memory, increasing <strong data-end=\"2437\" data-start=\"2411\">external fragmentation</strong>. First Fit may leave larger but more usable fragments.</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"2519\" data-start=\"2494\">&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"2517\" data-start=\"2497\">Mark Allocation:</strong></p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"2646\" data-start=\"2520\">\n\t<li data-end=\"2562\" data-start=\"2520\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2562\" data-start=\"2522\">Explanation of Best Fit behavior &ndash; 40%</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2597\" data-start=\"2563\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2597\" data-start=\"2565\">Concept of fragmentation &ndash; 40%</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2646\" data-start=\"2598\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2646\" data-start=\"2600\">Clarity of reasoning &ndash; 20%</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC202J",
   "LEVEL": 4,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO4"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Why does Best Fit sometimes result in more fragmentation than First Fit?</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 402,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 12514
  }
 ],
 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 12608,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"970\" data-start=\"659\">Contiguous memory allocation is one of the earliest memory management schemes used in operating systems. It involves <strong data-end=\"835\" data-start=\"776\">allocating a single contiguous block of physical memory</strong> to each process. (20%)<br data-end=\"855\" data-start=\"852\" />\nThe <strong data-end=\"884\" data-start=\"859\">Operating System (OS)</strong> maintains a <strong data-end=\"917\" data-start=\"897\">free memory list</strong>, and allocation is done based on certain strategies.</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"1098\" data-start=\"972\">When a process arrives, the OS selects a free block <strong data-end=\"1040\" data-start=\"1024\">large enough</strong> to accommodate it, using one of the following strategies:</p>\n\n<hr data-end=\"1103\" data-start=\"1100\" />\n<h3 data-end=\"1130\" data-start=\"1105\">\ud83d\udd38 <strong data-end=\"1128\" data-start=\"1112\">1. First Fit&nbsp;</strong> (30%)</h3>\n\n<ul data-end=\"1395\" data-start=\"1131\">\n\t<li data-end=\"1196\" data-start=\"1131\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1196\" data-start=\"1133\">Allocates the <strong data-end=\"1172\" data-start=\"1147\">first available block</strong> that is large enough.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1276\" data-start=\"1197\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1276\" data-start=\"1199\">It scans memory from the beginning and assigns the <strong data-end=\"1273\" data-start=\"1250\">first matching hole</strong>.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1314\" data-start=\"1277\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1314\" data-start=\"1279\"><strong data-end=\"1293\" data-start=\"1279\">Advantage:</strong> Fast; low overhead</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1395\" data-start=\"1315\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1395\" data-start=\"1317\"><strong data-end=\"1334\" data-start=\"1317\">Disadvantage:</strong> Can lead to many small unused holes (external fragmentation)</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr data-end=\"1400\" data-start=\"1397\" />\n<h3 data-end=\"1426\" data-start=\"1402\">\ud83d\udd38 <strong data-end=\"1424\" data-start=\"1409\">2. Best Fit </strong>(30%)</h3>\n\n<ul data-end=\"1669\" data-start=\"1427\">\n\t<li data-end=\"1482\" data-start=\"1427\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1482\" data-start=\"1429\">Allocates the <strong data-end=\"1460\" data-start=\"1443\">smallest hole</strong> that is big enough.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1546\" data-start=\"1483\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1546\" data-start=\"1485\">It searches the entire list and selects the <strong data-end=\"1543\" data-start=\"1529\">best match</strong>.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1588\" data-start=\"1547\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1588\" data-start=\"1549\"><strong data-end=\"1563\" data-start=\"1549\">Advantage:</strong> Minimizes wasted space</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1669\" data-start=\"1589\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1669\" data-start=\"1591\"><strong data-end=\"1608\" data-start=\"1591\">Disadvantage:</strong> Slower due to full search; may leave tiny unusable fragments</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr data-end=\"1674\" data-start=\"1671\" />\n<h3 data-end=\"1701\" data-start=\"1676\">\ud83d\udd38 <strong data-end=\"1699\" data-start=\"1683\">3. Worst Fit </strong>(20%)</h3>\n\n<ul data-end=\"1909\" data-start=\"1702\">\n\t<li data-end=\"1747\" data-start=\"1702\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1747\" data-start=\"1704\">Allocates the <strong data-end=\"1744\" data-start=\"1718\">largest available hole</strong>.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1804\" data-start=\"1748\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1804\" data-start=\"1750\">Idea is to leave large blocks behind for future use.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1850\" data-start=\"1805\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1850\" data-start=\"1807\"><strong data-end=\"1821\" data-start=\"1807\">Advantage:</strong> May avoid many small holes</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1909\" data-start=\"1851\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1909\" data-start=\"1853\"><strong data-end=\"1870\" data-start=\"1853\">Disadvantage:</strong> Often leads to inefficient space usage</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC202J",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Explain Contiguous Memory Allocation and its strategies. Compare the advantages and disadvantages of each strategy.</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 402,
   "TYPE": "lq",
   "key": 12608
  }
 ]
